{"id":"emergency-vendors","title":"Suppliers paid mostly under emergency powers","question":"Which suppliers received at least half of their City money since fiscal 2019 under emergency purchasing rules?","finding":"68 suppliers paid $1 million or more under emergency rules got at least half of all their City money that way ($489.4 million between them); for 42 it was 95% or more. The largest: Hotel Whitcomb ($62.8 million, 71%, fiscal 2020–2022); Color Health Inc. ($48.5 million, 59%, fiscal 2020–2022); Chinese Hospital Association ($29.1 million, 54%, fiscal 2020–2023); Off The Grid Services LLC ($28.7 million, 98%, fiscal 2020–2022).","how":"For each payee in the vendor-payment file, payments under a rule containing the word \"emergency\" divided by all payments to that payee, fiscal 2019 to fiscal 2027 to date. Listed when the emergency payments are $1 million or more and at least half of the total. The first and latest years are the fiscal years in which $10,000 or more was paid under such a rule, by the year each payment was issued, read from its voucher number. Other public bodies are left out.","limits":"Most of these are hotels, caterers, laboratories and suppliers of protective equipment hired for the pandemic response, which is what emergency powers are for; a supplier with no other City business will show 100%. The rows that ask a question are those still paid under emergency rules in fiscal 2025 or later. Payee names are as keyed, so one firm under two spellings is split. The payment file labels each line with a fiscal year that is not always the year the payment was issued: some earlier payments, mostly on purchase orders in multi-year capital funds, are filed under a later year, and the Controller's own published figures follow that label. Payments are dated here by voucher number, a single running sequence, which moves $5.52 billion of $119.3 billion (4.6%) to an earlier year than its label; $1.08 billion of that belongs to fiscal 2018 or earlier, before the file starts. Near the turn of a year the number dates a payment to within a few days. Payments that belong to fiscal 2018 or earlier are in none of the figures here.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"vendor","t":"Supplier","type":"org"},{"k":"kind","t":"Kind","type":"text"},{"k":"emergency","t":"Paid under emergency rules","type":"usd"},{"k":"all","t":"All City payments","type":"usd"},{"k":"share","t":"Share","type":"pct"},{"k":"first","t":"First year","type":"year"},{"k":"last","t":"Latest year","type":"year"},{"k":"years","t":"Years","type":"int"},{"k":"departments","t":"Departments","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"emergency":62757735,"all":88149569,"share":0.7119,"first":2020,"last":2022,"years":3,"departments":"Human Services Agency","kind":"business","vendor":"Hotel Whitcomb","vendorKey":null},{"emergency":48545230,"all":81744902,"share":0.5939,"first":2020,"last":2022,"years":3,"departments":"Public Health","kind":"business","vendor":"Color Health Inc.","vendorKey":null},{"emergency":29125970,"all":54307364,"share":0.5363,"first":2020,"last":2023,"years":4,"departments":"Public Health","kind":"nonprofit","vendor":"Chinese Hospital Association","vendorKey":"CHINESE HOSPITAL ASSOCIATION"},{"emergency":28708781,"all":29243503,"share":0.9817,"first":2020,"last":2022,"years":3,"departments":"Human Services Agency","kind":"business","vendor":"Off The Grid Services LLC","vendorKey":null},{"emergency":26512650,"all":47132850,"share":0.5625,"first":2021,"last":2027,"years":7,"departments":"Homelessness Services","kind":"nonprofit","vendor":"Providence Foundation Of San Francisco","vendorKey":"PROVIDENCE FOUNDATION SAN FRANCISCO"},{"emergency":15039955,"all":15063955,"share":0.9984,"first":2020,"last":2021,"years":2,"departments":"Public Health","kind":"business","vendor":"Fam LLC","vendorKey":null},{"emergency":12092091,"all":21040143,"share":0.5747,"first":2020,"last":2022,"years":3,"departments":"Human Services Agency","kind":"business","vendor":"Americania Hotel